+    # BELOW ONE CENT, DOLLARS TO TWO PLACES RENDER "about $0.00", AND THAT READS
+    # AS A CLAIM THAT THE WORK WAS FREE. Sanaa has ruled that cost transparency
+    # is a rule and that the compute line is KEPT, so the repair is to make the
+    # number LEGIBLE and never to drop it. The same derived figure in cents is
+    # legible at this magnitude and the quantity is not touched: 1.9
+    # processor-minutes is $0.0016, which is 0.2 cents.
+    #
+    # THE THRESHOLD SITS WHERE THE TWO RENDERINGS ALREADY AGREE, so this is not
+    # a change to what any existing act shows. Measured rather than asserted:
+    # every run at or above 5.85 core-minutes renders BYTE-IDENTICALLY to what
+    # it renders today. The jet-flap act costs 117.5 core-minutes and shows
+    # "about $0.10"; that sentence is unchanged to the byte, 20x above the line.
+    money = (f"about ${usd:,.2f}" if usd >= 0.005
+             else f"about {usd * 100:.1f} cents")
     return (f"Compute used: {cm:,.1f} {SCREEN_COMPUTE_UNIT} ({basis}), "
-            f"about ${usd:,.2f}, derived at the recorded rate.")
+            f"{money}, derived at the recorded rate.")
 
 
